The save effect runs immediately on mount even when the collapsed state hasn't changed from the default. This will write 'false' to localStorage on first visit, which is unnecessary. Consider only saving to localStorage when the user actually toggles the state, or check if the value differs from the loaded value before saving. This will reduce unnecessary localStorage writes and improve performance.
```suggestion
  const initialCollapsedRef = React.useRef(isEditorCollapsed);

  // Load collapsed state from localStorage
  useEffect(() => {
    if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {
      const savedState = localStorage.getItem('playground-editor-collapsed');
      if (savedState) {
        const collapsed = savedState === 'true';
        setIsEditorCollapsed(collapsed);
        initialCollapsedRef.current = collapsed;
      } else {
        // No saved state; use the current default as the initial value
        initialCollapsedRef.current = isEditorCollapsed;
      }
    }
  }, []);

  // Save collapsed state to localStorage
  useEffect(() => {
    if (typeof window === 'undefined') {
      return;
    }

    // Only persist when the value has changed from the initially loaded value
    if (isEditorCollapsed === initialCollapsedRef.current) {
      return;
    }

    localStorage.setItem('playground-editor-collapsed', String(isEditorCollapsed));
```
